    {
      "id": 6,
      "name": "Food and beverage services",
      "definition": "Food and beverage offerings within the parks, including restaurants, dining options, prices, and perceptions of food quality and value for money.",
      "reviews": [
        "Food can be expensive if you choose to eat in the park, and options are fairly limited (mostly burgers, chicken, or fish), unless you choose to go to one of the proper restaurants for a sit-down meal.",
        "The Hunters Grill restaurant was nice, with a good choice of food and tasty dishes, but very expensive; four soft drinks and four meals cost over 100 euros, although, to be honest, these are average prices for all the restaurants at Disney.",
        "Food options are very limited, with a few corn on the cob, hot dog, popcorn, and candy floss stalls, and overcrowded restaurants selling mediocre Chinese and Western food."
